wlanpi-core (2.3.18-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Find a config's radio by its interface name first, and by its display
    name only if no interface has that name, so a display name that another
    radio already carries no longer selects that radio (#236).
  * When a prepare fails, only remove a half-created interface if it is on
    the radio being prepared. Previously a rename that failed because
    another radio owned the name deleted that other radio's interface.

 -- Ben Toner <ben@numerousnetworks.co.uk>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:39:28 -0500

wlanpi-core (2.3.17-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Write wpa_supplicant values so they round-trip exactly (#278).
    wpa_supplicant reads a "quoted" value literally up to the last quote,
    so the backslash escaping Core used changed any SSID or passphrase
    containing a quote or backslash. SSIDs are now written as hex,
    passphrases unescaped in quotes (or a 64-hex PSK bare), and EAP
    identity, password and certificate paths as printf-escaped P"...".
  * Reject a WPA2 PSK that is not 8-63 printable ASCII characters or 64 hex
    digits, and a WPA3 PSK that is not a passphrase, with 422 instead of
    failing when wpa_supplicant starts.

 -- Ben Toner <ben@numerousnetworks.co.uk>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:32:46 -0500

wlanpi-core (2.3.16-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Replace dhclient, which Trixie does not ship, with dhcpcd (#261). Each
    dhcpcd runs in a private mount namespace with its own state under
    /run/wlanpi-core/dhcpcd/<netns>/<iface>, so the same interface name in
    two namespaces gets two leases, and is released and stopped by PID.
    No IPv4 link-local fallback; the hostname and timesyncd hooks are off,
    and in root so is the resolv.conf hook.
  * Never install a gatewayless default route: default_route uses the DHCP
    router, and adds nothing when there is none (#279).
  * Starting a connection monitor stops the previous one for the same
    interface, a superseded monitor no longer deregisters its successor,
    and a stop request is honoured before DHCP, route and app start.

 -- Ben Toner <ben@numerousnetworks.co.uk>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 21:58:51 -0500

wlanpi-core (2.3.15-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Write network profiles and current.txt atomically (temp file, fsync,
    rename), so a crash or full disk never leaves a truncated profile. New
    profile files are created 0600 (#277).
  * Deleting the active profile with force now deactivates it first, so
    current.txt never names a deleted profile; without force it is still
    refused with 409.
  * Reject the configuration IDs default, root and status in any letter
    case with 400.

