wlanpi-core (2.3.11-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Only return and delete network namespaces Core created, recorded by a
    marker under /run/wlanpi-core/netns. Deactivate no longer moves radios
    out of, or deletes, namespaces created by users or other tools (#275).
  * Return namespaces to root by walking their phys rather than their
    interfaces, so a phy with no netdev, or several netdevs, comes back, and
    delete a namespace only once no phys or links remain in it.
  * A namespace created by an earlier Core version has no marker, so it is
    not deleted until reboot. A phy returned without a netdev stays in root
    with no interface until a profile or a tool creates one.

