wlanpi-core (2.1.21-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Raise the capture subscriber queue budget (128 to 1024 blocks) and send
    timeout (1.0s to 5.0s) so a subscriber survives transient stalls on a
    busy channel instead of being dropped. At the about 2800 packets/s
    measured on a busy 5 GHz channel the new budget is about 0.37s, versus
    about 46ms before.
